### init

Source: https://threejs.org/docs/pages/GPUComputationRenderer.html

Initializes the renderer.

```APIDOC
## .init()

### Description
Initializes the renderer. Returns null if successful, or an error message string if an error occurs.
```

### Methods > .onBeforeCompile()

Source: https://threejs.org/docs/pages/Material.html

The onBeforeCompile callback provides a way to modify built-in materials by accessing the shader source code before compilation. While useful for WebGLRenderer, the recommended approach for modern material customization is to use WebGPURenderer with the Node Material system and TSL.

--------------------------------

### ShaderMaterial > Notes

Source: https://threejs.org/docs/pages/ShaderMaterial.html

When using ShaderMaterial, note that it is exclusively compatible with WebGLRenderer. By default, the material automatically passes built-in attributes and uniforms to the shaders; if this behavior is not desired, RawShaderMaterial should be used instead.
